# core.autocrlf=true (Git for Windows' default) checks text out with CRLF, which
# breaks shell scripts under WSL and Linux shells sharing the checkout. Skill
# frontmatter also stays byte-identical everywhere: the installer's SHA-256
# manifests must match any checkout, so the SKILL.md files keep LF too.
*.sh text eol=lf
skills/**/SKILL.md text eol=lf
